# Requests for the Sentinel API. Open in Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code
# (REST Client extension) and click "Send Request" above each one.
# The X-Demo-User header is the development-only identity (Chapter 12).

@api = http://localhost:5080
@admin = ada.okafor@sentinel.dev

### Who am I?
GET {{api}}/api/me
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### My menu (try with and without the header)
GET {{api}}/api/me/navigation
X-Demo-User: emeka.nwosu@sentinel.dev

### May Emeka open the ledger export? (no: explicitly denied)
GET {{api}}/api/me/page-access?path=/reports/finance/export
X-Demo-User: emeka.nwosu@sentinel.dev

### Is my account safe?
GET {{api}}/api/me/security
X-Demo-User: tunde.bakare@sentinel.dev

### Simulate the identity provider: a failed sign-in from Frankfurt
POST {{api}}/api/sign-ins
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "femi.bello@sentinel.dev",
  "occurredAt": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "ipAddress": "185.220.101.9",
  "userAgent": "curl/8.9.1",
  "succeeded": false,
  "failureReason": "WrongPassword"
}

### A timestamp without a zone is accepted by DateTimeOffset as LOCAL time
### on the server. Compare with the request above and read Chapter 22.
POST {{api}}/api/sign-ins
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "femi.bello@sentinel.dev",
  "occurredAt": "2026-10-25T09:00:00",
  "ipAddress": "185.220.101.9",
  "succeeded": true
}

### Validation problem (400 with one entry per field)
POST {{api}}/api/users
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "", "displayName": "", "timeZoneId": "Africa/Lagos" }

### Forbidden: an auditor may read users but not create them
POST {{api}}/api/users
X-Demo-User: femi.bello@sentinel.dev
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "new.person@sentinel.dev", "displayName": "New Person", "timeZoneId": "Africa/Lagos" }
